                <pb facs="0803" n="793" sameAs="frus:frus1937v05/pg793"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.3131/145: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Venezuela</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Nicholson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-11-27T15:00:00-05:00">November 27, 1937—3
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>67. Your despatch no. 870, November 13. The Department does not intend to add to
                    its tentative list of products on which concessions <pb facs="0804" n="794"
                        xml:id="pg794"/> are desired, prior to the holding of public hearings
                    following the next public announcement, but it has no objection to the
                    Venezuelan Government revising within the next few days the list which it is now
                    presenting to you. You should say to the Venezuelan authorities, however, that
                    it is hoped that the Venezuelan Government may find it possible to expedite any
                    revision of its list in order that the second public announcement may be made at
                    an early date.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
